    {
      "id": 38,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -620,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        560,
        1180
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 37,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## LTX-2.5 + LTX Director (GGUF, 1-Stage or 2-Stage) - RTX 3090\n\n### Required custom nodes\n- `ComfyUI-GGUF` (`city96/ComfyUI-GGUF`)\n- `WhatDreamsCost-ComfyUI` (`WhatDreamsCost/WhatDreamsCost-ComfyUI`, latest v2.0+ with LTX Director)\n- Up-to-date ComfyUI + `ComfyUI-LTXVideo`\n\n### How to use 3+ guiding images in LTX Director\n1. Drag & drop **3 or more images** directly onto the **LTX Director** timeline track.\n2. Position each image where you want it to appear (e.g. Start at 0s, Middle at 4s, End at 8s).\n   Right-click the final image block -> **Pin as End Frame** so it lands on the exact last frame.\n3. Write a **global prompt** (scene/characters/lighting) and a **per-segment prompt** for each block (Prompt Relay automatically scopes each prompt to its time range).\n4. **Audio**: leave `use_custom_audio` OFF to let LTX-2.5 generate synchronized audio/dialogue, OR drag a voice/music clip onto the audio track and turn `use_custom_audio` ON (`inpaint_audio` fills empty gaps).\n\n### 1-Stage vs 2-Stage (`RUN STAGE 2?` toggle)\n- **ON (default, 2-stage):** Stage 1 automatically runs at **0.5x** (`512x512` for a `1024x1024` target), then Stage 2 runs the learned 2x latent upscaler + 3 refinement steps back to full target size.\n- **OFF (1-stage):** Stage 1 automatically switches to **1.0x** and skips Stage 2 completely. Lower `custom_width`/`custom_height` inside Director (e.g. `768x768` or `768x448`) for fast 1-stage runs on 24 GB VRAM.\n- Keep `divisible_by = 64` in Director so both 1x and 0.5x sizes are divisible by 32.\n- Keep `ltx-2.5-latent-spatial-upscaler-x2-bf16-1.0.safetensors` installed & selected even when Stage 2 is OFF (ComfyUI validates connected loaders).\n\n### Continuing into a longer scene\n- Every run also saves the **last decoded frame PNG** (`video/LTX25_Director_last_frame_*`). Drop it at 0s of a new Director timeline to continue the next clip.\n"
      ],
      "title": "READ ME - LTX-2.5 Director Workflow",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 39,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1220,
        0
      ],
      "size": [
        560,
        1180
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 38,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "HOW TO: Length, Resolution & 3+ Images",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## QUICK GUIDE: Length, Resolution & 3+ Images (LTX Director)\n\n### 1. How to change LENGTH (duration)\n- Inside the **LTX Director** node (Group 3):\n  - Set **`duration_seconds`** (e.g. `5`, `8`, `10`) or drag the timeline end handle.\n  - Keep **`frame_rate = 24`**. Director auto-snaps frames to **`8n + 1`** (`5s=121`, `8s=193`, `10s=241`).\n\n### 2. How to change RESOLUTION\n- Inside the **LTX Director** node:\n  - Set **`custom_width`** and **`custom_height`** to your **FINAL target size** (or `0` and `0` to match your first image).\n  - Keep **`divisible_by = 64`** (so both 1\u00d7 and 0.5\u00d7 stay divisible by 32).\n  - **`RUN STAGE 2? = ON`** -> Stage 1 auto-scales to **0.5\u00d7**, Stage 2 refines \u00d72 back to full target size!\n  - **`RUN STAGE 2? = OFF`** -> Stage 1 auto-scales to **1.0\u00d7** (1-stage) and skips Stage 2!\n\n| Aspect | 2-Stage ON (set in Director) | 1-Stage OFF (set in Director) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1:1 Square | `1024\u00d71024` (S1 runs `512\u00d7512`) | `768\u00d7768` or `512\u00d7512` |\n| 16:9 Wide | `1536\u00d7896` (S1 runs `768\u00d7448`) | `768\u00d7448` or `896\u00d7512` |\n| 16:9 1080p | `1920\u00d71088` (S1 runs `960\u00d7544`) | use 2-Stage ON on 3090 |\n| 9:16 Vertical | `896\u00d71536` (S1 runs `448\u00d7768`) | `448\u00d7768` or `512\u00d7896` |\n\n### 3. How to use 3, 4, or more guiding images\n1. **Drag & drop** your images directly onto the Director timeline track.\n2. Slide each image to its timestamp (e.g. Start `0s`, Mid `4s`, End `8s`).\n3. Right-click the final image block -> **Pin as End Frame** (locks to exact last frame).\n4. Write a **Global Prompt** (characters/style/lighting) + a **Segment Prompt** per block (Prompt Relay scopes each prompt to its time slice).\n\n### 4. Audio & Multi-Clip Continuation\n- **Model-generated audio (default):** leave `use_custom_audio = false`.\n- **Custom voice/music:** drag audio onto the audio track, turn `use_custom_audio = true` (`inpaint_audio = true` fills empty gaps).\n- **Next clip:** every run saves `video/LTX25_Director_last_frame_*.png` \u2014 drag it to `0s` of a new run to continue.\n\n### 5. If Out of Memory (3090 24 GB)\n1. Lower `VAEDecodeTiled` `tile_size`: `512` -> `384` -> `256`.\n2. In both `LTXDirectorGuide` nodes, toggle `use_tiled_encode = true`.\n3. Reduce `custom_width`/`custom_height` or `duration_seconds`.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    }
